  "notes": "Imported 12.08.2026 from a beamline jcpds collection. Source file(s): JCPDS/dac_user_jcpds/Fe3S-Fei.jcpds, JCPDS/dac_user_jcpds/Fe3S_calc.jcpds. Fei et al., American Mineralogist 85, 1830-1833 (2000), doi:10.2138/am-2000-11-1229, identify the phase as Fe3P-type I-4; the reported cell and density imply Z=8. The atom sites are an explicitly approximate Fe3P-type proxy based on the near-end-member Fe3P schreibersite refinement Htr of Britvin et al., American Mineralogist 106, 1520-1529 (2021), doi:10.2138/am-2021-7766: its P site is replaced by S while the three Fe sites are retained. These coordinates were not refined for the Fe3S specimen and must not be presented as its original structure; calculated intensities are approximate, while the legacy Fe3S peaks remain authoritative where available.",
